Preconditions confirmed before implementation:
- The branch was rebased onto current origin/master after T18A merged.
- T18A.done existed.
- IIdentityDirectory.FindUserByIdAsync(Guid userId, CancellationToken) existed.
- The authoritative PRD, architecture, and tasks.md recorded the two-stage
  tenancy-bootstrap authorization decision.
- Every earlier-wave marker through T18A.done existed.
- The branch was clean and had no commits beyond origin/master, so no T19
  implementation had previously been committed.

Delivered authorization behavior:
- Cookie authentication first resolves and evaluates the live, unrevoked,
  in-bounds durable session through the existing T18 key-only ticket store.
- Bootstrap GET /firms and POST /firms/select then reload PortalUser by the
  session-derived UserId, require the user to remain active, and reload active
  memberships from IIdentityDirectory on every request.
- Bootstrap permits ActiveFirmId to be null; the separately registered
  firm-scoped policy additionally requires one active membership matching the
  session-derived UserId and ActiveFirmId.
- Identity and membership exceptions, cancellations, missing rows, inactive
  rows, malformed server-derived claims, and mismatches fail closed with a
  fixed response and no record content.
- GET /firms renders only active firm display names and opaque membership
  identifiers, plus the antiforgery token required for selection.
- POST /firms/select accepts only membershipId plus the antiforgery token,
  verifies that the active membership belongs to the authenticated session
  user, and reads no firm identifier from any request channel.
- Selection recovers issuer and subject from the freshly loaded local
  PortalUser, passes them through T18's existing local-principal resolution,
  rechecks the user and active memberships, revokes the prior session, and
  issues a new session through the existing T18 SessionTicketStore.
- The replacement session has a new SessionId, its own freshly derived idle
  and absolute boundaries, and the selected trusted ActiveFirmId.
- The replacement browser cookie retains T18's protected key-only shape and
  carries no UserId, FirmId, issuer, subject, token, or claims payload.
- Missing and foreign membership selectors produce the same status and body.
- The exact route, input, authorization-file, registration, and portal-source
  allowlists were updated without opening any taxpayer-data surface.

